---
import WysFrame from '../../../components/WysFrame.astro';
import WysPhoto from '../../../components/WysPhoto.astro';
import {WYS_ROOT,examples,imageNotice} from '../../../data/wys.js';
const selected={ 'pretty-wicked-entryway':['Plain hot-pink ribbed pumpkins','Pink open-weave gauze','Pink jack-o-lantern string lights','Black folded-wing bat decorations','Pink LED tea lights'], 'ghoul-fuel-coffee-bar':['Pink sculpted ghost mug','Pink two-tier heart serving stand','Mini velvet pumpkins','Pink LED tea lights','Small silver mirror balls'] };
---
<WysFrame current="inside" title="Look Inside the While-You-Sleep Storefront™ | TDIE" description="Explore two approved TDIE styling examples through their basic, styled and lifestyle photographs, with selected pieces and preparation details." ogImage={examples[1].photos[1].src.src}>
 <header class="wys-wrap wys-section wys-inside-hero"><div><p class="wys-ribbon">Look inside the styling process</p><h1>One idea.<br/>Three ways to <em>bring it to life.</em></h1><p class="wys-lede">Explore the actual approved photographs behind Pretty Wicked and Ghoul Fuel. See the selected pieces, the styled scene and the separately composed lifestyle moment.</p><div class="wys-actions"><a class="wys-button" href="#pretty-wicked-entryway">Explore Pretty Wicked <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="wys-text-link" href="#ghoul-fuel-coffee-bar">Jump to Ghoul Fuel <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><p class="wys-small-copy">These are styling examples from Jodie’s workflow. This preview does not unlock the customer kit or demonstrate every buyer path.</p></div><div class="wys-inside-cover"><WysPhoto photo={examples[1].photos[1]} treatment="double" caption="Ghoul Fuel · the styled coffee nook" eager/><span class="wys-paper-tag">The actual approved images</span></div></header>
 {examples.map((example,index)=><section class:list={['wys-example-band',{'wys-example-lavender':index===1}]} id={example.slug} aria-labelledby={`${example.slug}-heading`}><div class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wys-section-head"><div><p class="wys-label">0{index+1} / {example.category}</p><h2 id={`${example.slug}-heading`}>{example.name}<em>.</em></h2></div><p>Switch between the complete photographs, then explore what belongs to the shopping list and what is a styling extra.</p></div><div class="wys-example-layout"><div class="wys-viewer" data-wys-viewer><div class="wys-view-tabs" aria-label={`${example.name} photographs`}>{example.photos.map((photo,i)=><button type="button" id={`${example.slug}-tab-${i}`} data-view={i} aria-controls={`${example.slug}-view-${i}`} aria-pressed={i===0}>{photo.role}</button>)}</div><div class="wys-view-panels">{example.photos.map((photo,i)=><div id={`${example.slug}-view-${i}`} class="wys-view-panel" data-panel={i} aria-labelledby={`${example.slug}-tab-${i}`}><WysPhoto photo={photo} treatment={['pink','arch','double'][i]} label={photo.role}/></div>)}</div></div><div class="wys-example-notes"><div class="wys-note-sheet"><p class="wys-label">The selected pieces</p><h3>Five product types,<br/>one styling idea.</h3><ul class="wys-selected">{selected[example.slug].map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p class="wys-small-copy">Affiliate links and Amazon Idea Lists for this example are pending. Furniture, clothing, flowers and other props are styling extras.</p><a class="wys-button" href={`/lifestyle/${example.slug}`}>Read the full styling article <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="wys-ticket"><span class="wys-label">The viewpoint matters</span><p>{index===0?'The lifestyle view is photographed from the porch, through the open door. It shows a natural Halloween greeting rather than a person pasted into the console photograph.':'The lifestyle view shows Tommy Kate holding and stirring one ghost mug beside the counter. It changes the framing and action while keeping the coffee nook recognizable.'}</p></div></div></div><p class="wys-image-notice">{imageNotice}</p></div></section>)}
 <section class="wys-section wys-wrap"><div class="wys-section-head"><div><p class="wys-ribbon wys-ribbon-lavender">What happens after the photos</p><h2>Pretty is the start.<br/><em>Review is part of the process.</em></h2></div><p>The photographs become separate Pin drafts with deterministic typography. The source photographs stay unchanged.</p></div><div class="wys-review-grid"><article class="wys-note-sheet"><span class="wys-number">01</span><h3>Prepare the destination</h3><p>Verify the exact look’s Idea List or owned website page. A sourcing URL is not a verified affiliate destination.</p></article><article class="wys-ticket"><span class="wys-number">02</span><h3>Check the finished draft</h3><p>Review the image, title, alt text, disclosure, destination and actual public board before authorizing a schedule.</p></article><article class="wys-kit-item"><span class="wys-number">03</span><h3>Record the real status</h3><p>Prepared, scheduled, published and verified are separate states. A successful build does not prove publication.</p></article></div></section>
 <section class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wys-invitation wys-invitation-compact"><div><p class="wys-label">Keep exploring</p><h2>Your next pretty idea<br/><em>has a place to start.</em></h2><p>Browse the Lifestyle articles or follow TDIE updates. The customer kit is on hold, with no checkout or delivery release.</p><div class="wys-actions"><a class="wys-button" href={WYS_ROOT+'/waitlist'}>Stay in the loop <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="wys-text-link" href="/lifestyle">Explore Lifestyle <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div><WysPhoto photo={examples[0].photos[2]} treatment="polaroid" caption="Pretty Wicked · the porch-door view"/></div></section>
</WysFrame>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-wys-viewer]').forEach(viewer=>{
  const buttons=Array.from(viewer.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-view]'));
  const panels=Array.from(viewer.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-panel]'));
  const show=(index:number)=>{buttons.forEach((button,i)=>button.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(i===index)));panels.forEach((panel,i)=>panel.hidden=i!==index);};
  buttons.forEach((button,index)=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>show(index)));
  show(0);
 });
</script>
